# <%= @module_name %>

A Breeze terminal application served over SSH, generated by `breeze_new`.

## Run over SSH in development

Fetch dependencies and generate a development-only SSH host key once:

```bash
mix deps.get
mix termite.ssh.gen_host_key
```

Start the SSH listener:

```bash
mix run
```

Development binds to `localhost:2222` with authentication explicitly
disabled. Connect with:

```bash
ssh -o PreferredAuthentications=none -o PubkeyAuthentication=no -p 2222 demo@localhost
```

Each connection gets an independent view. <%= if @theme_cycle do %>Press `F3` to cycle themes and
`q` to close the current SSH session.<% else %>Press `q` to close the current SSH session.<% end %>

## Run the view locally

Use the same view directly in your terminal without starting the SSH
listener:

```bash
mix <%= @app_name %>.local
```

<%= @render_cache_readme %>

<%= if @timeline do %>
## Timeline inspector

Development records each rendered state with `breeze_timeline`. With the
application still running, open another terminal in this project and run:

```bash
mix breeze.inspector
```

Select a checkpoint to preview it, or press `Enter` to rewind the running
application to that state. Timeline recording is disabled in production.
<% end %>

## Production authentication

Production refuses to start unless host keys and public-key authentication
are configured. Set these runtime variables:

```bash
export <%= @env_prefix %>_SSH_USER=alice
export <%= @env_prefix %>_SSH_AUTHORIZED_KEYS_DIR=/srv/<%= @app_name %>/users/alice
export <%= @env_prefix %>_SSH_SYSTEM_DIR=/srv/<%= @app_name %>/host_keys
export <%= @env_prefix %>_SSH_PORT=2222 # optional
MIX_ENV=prod mix run
```

`<%= @env_prefix %>_SSH_AUTHORIZED_KEYS_DIR` must name a directory containing
an OpenSSH-compatible `authorized_keys` or `authorized_keys2` file.
`<%= @env_prefix %>_SSH_SYSTEM_DIR` must contain a provisioned
`ssh_host_*_key`; do not reuse the generated development key in production.

See the
[Termite.SSH authentication documentation](https://termite-ssh.hexdocs.pm/0.1.0/Termite.SSH.html#module-authentication)
before exposing the listener publicly.

## Test

```bash
mix test
```

Tests do not start a listener; the view is exercised through `Breeze.Test`.

<%= if @storybook do %>
## Storybook

The starter includes a function component and an interactive story:

```bash
mix breeze.storybook
```
<% end %>
